The format marks the file manager draws on a file's page come from devicon too,
under the same MIT License: apache.svg, bash.svg, cmake.svg, cplusplus.svg,
csharp.svg, css3.svg, dart.svg, elixir.svg, haskell.svg, html5.svg, java.svg,
javascript.svg, json.svg, kotlin.svg, latex.svg, lua.svg, markdown.svg,
perl.svg, php.svg, pnpm.svg, powershell.svg, r.svg, react.svg, ruby.svg,
rust.svg, sass.svg, scala.svg, svelte.svg, swift.svg, tailwindcss.svg,
typescript.svg, vitejs.svg, vuejs.svg, xml.svg, yaml.svg, yarn.svg and zig.svg
are its <name>-original.svg and graphql.svg its graphql-plain.svg, unchanged;
c.svg is c-original.svg as of devicon v2.15.1, whose hexagon reads on a page
where the later letterform's pale grey does not.

pnpm-light.svg is devicon's pnpm-original.svg, as pnpm.svg is, with its
charcoal #4c4c4c lifted to #a4a4a4, the same grey at the L 0.72 rung, for the
tile a package manager is drawn on; pnpm.svg stays as it was for the file
manager's paper page.

The database engines the Databases pages draw — the products a driver talks
to under another name, and the servers found on a machine that the dashboard
cannot open — come from the same three collections.

From homarr-labs/dashboard-icons, under the Apache License 2.0: etcd.svg and
couchdb.svg keep their names and are unchanged. cassandra.svg is its
apache-cassandra.svg with the charcoal #373535 of the eye's lids and lashes
lifted to #a6a4a4; opensearch.svg had both of its blues lifted, #003b5c to
#77abd2 and #005eb8 to #60a7ff; and ferretdb.svg had its navy #092032 lifted
to #8ea8c0, and the drawing program's ids, class and style element folded into
one fill attribute — each the same hue at the L 0.72 rung, so the mark reads
on a dark ground. kafka.svg is its kafka-dark.svg, the white mark it draws for
a dark theme, without the XML declaration, title, role and fixed size that
file carries.

From devicon v2.17.0, under the MIT License above: nats.svg and yugabytedb.svg
are its nats-original.svg and yugabytedb-original.svg, and memcached.svg its
memcached-plain.svg, unchanged. elasticsearch.svg is its
elasticsearch-original.svg, the engine's own three bands — the file
dashboard-icons ships under that name is its elastic.svg, the company's mark —
with the charcoal #343741 of the middle band lifted to #a0a4b0, the same hue
at the L 0.72 rung, and the file's indentation removed.

From Simple Icons 16.33.0 (https://simpleicons.org), CC0 1.0, without the title
and role its files carry and filled because Simple Icons ships the path alone:
timescaledb.svg (its timescale.svg), tidb.svg, scylladb.svg and duckdb.svg in
their brand colour (#FDB515, #DC150B, #6CD5E7, #FFF000); cockroachdb.svg (its
cockroachlabs.svg) in its #6933FF lifted to #9b95ff; and neo4j.svg, the mark
Neo4j uses now where dashboard-icons draws the disc it retired, in its #4581C3
lifted to #6ba8ed — both the same hue at the L 0.72 rung. scylladb.svg is a
hairline outline, the only rendition any of the three collections has, and is
faint as the smallest glyph on a screen of ordinary density; it is left as the
collection draws it rather than thickened by hand.

Azure SQL Edge has no file: none of the three collections draws it a mark of
its own, and it is drawn with sqlserver.svg, the engine it is. Percona Server,
KeyDB and Dragonfly are in none of the three either and have no logo here; the
pages draw them with a plain database glyph rather than another product's mark.

mono/ holds the single-colour marks pressed into a folder's face. Every file
there is from Simple Icons (https://simpleicons.org), CC0 1.0, unchanged, renamed
after the product key the folders use: nodedotjs.svg is nodejs.svg,
nextdotjs.svg nextjs.svg, letsencrypt.svg lets-encrypt.svg, rubygems.svg
ruby.svg, openjdk.svg java.svg, visualstudiocode.svg vscode.svg and gnubash.svg
bash.svg.

The Network pages draw the tunnels, resolvers and intrusion tools a server
runs. From homarr-labs/dashboard-icons, under the Apache License 2.0:
adguard-home.svg, pi-hole.svg and zerotier.svg are unchanged. wireguard.svg had
its near-black #231f20 lifted to #a8a3a4, crowdsec.svg its purples #3e3978 and
#4e4a99 to #9c9ce4 and #999af1, headscale.svg its #303030 to #a4a4a4,
mullvad.svg its navy #192e45 to #8ea7c4, unbound.svg its #2d2e83 to #8e9bfb and
openvpn.svg its #1a3967 to #82a6dc — each the same hue at the L 0.72 rung, so
the mark reads on a dark ground. quad9.svg is Simple Icons' path (CC0) filled
with the brand's #DC205E.
